# /etc/exports.d/racesow.exports on the EU box. Then: exportfs -ra
# docs/map-store-runbook.md, step C.
#
# The export is the bind mount /srv/racesow/store (fstab.eu.example), not
# ~/racesow/server/maps itself: with all_squash the reader is the anonymous
# user, which would need execute permission on the deploy user's home
# directory (usually 0750) to reach a path under it.
#
#   ro              readers never write; only the EU box adds or removes packs
#   all_squash      the reader is anonymous; packs are world-readable already
#                   (fetch-maps.sh and the mapgen worker both write them 0644)
#   no_subtree_check  the export is a whole directory; skip the per-request walk
#   sec=sys         the tunnel is the authentication; one /32 peer, nothing else
#   10.66.0.2/32    the US box's WireGuard address, and nothing else
/srv/racesow/store 10.66.0.2/32(ro,all_squash,no_subtree_check,sec=sys)
